[# docs-src/repos/cx-platform-workbench.cxd — the workbench's page,
   repo-cx-platform-workbench.html (cx-private#1855, from #750; RULED:
   DOCS-41, DOCS-49). Facts from the registries; the one example from its own
   corpus (the workbench smoke case). #]

[repo name=cx-platform-workbench
  [intro
    """One place to open a CX document, read it, talk about it and change it
       without breaking it. `cx-platform-workbench` is the document
       workbench: it browses a document by path or CXPath, keeps comments on
       its nodes beside it, and makes every edit a previewed change whose
       result is checked — it re-reads to its own address and passes its
       declared schema — before a byte of the file is written."""]
  [body
    """The workbench is a consumer of verbs cx already ships: the strict
       canonical form and its hash give every node and every version an
       identity, CXPath selects, the semantic diff shows what an edit does,
       schema validation decides whether it may land, and the lossless
       formatter keeps the bytes a person wrote. A comment is itself a CX
       element, addressed by the hashes of the document and of the node it is
       about, so it survives a reformat and is refused when its node is gone."""]
  [gives
    """One package of the platform group, born as its own repository rather
       than extracted from the front door. Today it carries its design and
       its first conformance case; the module and its `cx` subcommand land
       with the implementation."""]
  [try
    """The comment shape, frozen by the design: a comment on node /2/1 of a
       document, read back as its head, its attribute names in order and its
       one body."""]
  [fixture id=wb-000-the-comment-shape]
  [status
    """A design with its error band registered (CXER7300–7349) and one smoke
       case graded by the repository's own check; the module, its reference
       page and its place in the build arrive with the implementation."""]]
